<rtept lat="51.3913980000" lon="-1.1496980000">
<time>2026-05-29T13:18:52Z</time>
<name>Basingstoke Road to End</name>
<desc><![CDATA[Cross over Basingstoke Road (this is a busy road, so take particular care here) and turn left along the narrow verge for just 300 yards until you reach a gravel pull-in with metal gates. Turn right here alongside a disused stile signed as a footpath. Follow the footpath along the left-hand edge of an open field, cross over the footbridge over the River Enbornel, and cross diagonally over the next field. 

Soon, the path will be running directly alongside the main branch of the River Kennet on the right. Keep your eyes peeled for wildlife here, as this section of the river is home to a range of rare species supported by the chalk watercourse. 

On the right, you'll pass Froud's Bridge marina. Further along, you'll reach the large footbridge you crossed earlier. Pass alongside this and keep ahead to join the stone towpath. From this point, simply keep ahead, retracing your steps alongside the canal to reach the trailhead.]]></desc>
